---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../components/SectionLabel.astro';
import PowerBench from '../../components/PowerBench.astro';
import Icon from '../../components/Icon.astro';
---
<Base title="The workbench" description="Try a hardware power-budget model, then inspect a broken tool schema. Two small experiments you can run in your browser.">
  <section class="page-intro container">
    <SectionLabel number="02" label="THE LAB" extra="TWO BROWSER EXPERIMENTS" />
    <h1>WELCOME TO<br /><em>THE WORKBENCH.</em></h1>
    <div class="page-intro-bottom"><p>A couple of things to play with: a simplified power-and-cooling model, and a tool-schema bug you can inspect and repair.</p><span class="mono">HARDWARE THINKING / SOFTWARE EXPERIMENTS</span></div>
  </section>
  <nav class="lab-jump-links container" aria-label="Lab experiments">
    <a href="#power-bench"><span class="mono">01</span>Power budget <Icon name="chip" /></a>
    <a href="#schema-bench"><span class="mono">02</span>Schema check <Icon name="crosshair" /></a>
  </nav>
  <div class="container"><PowerBench /></div>
  <section class="container lab-page-section" id="schema-bench" aria-labelledby="experiment-title">
    <div class="experiment-heading">
      <div><span class="mono">BENCH / 02 — DEVELOPER TOOLS</span><h2 id="experiment-title">ONE MISSING<br /><em>DEFINITION.</em></h2></div>
      <a class="text-link" href="/work/schema-sentinel/">Read about SchemaSentinel <Icon /></a>
    </div>
    <p class="experiment-description">The <code>get_weather</code> tool refers to <code>#/$defs/Location</code>. In the first example, that definition is missing. Compare it with the repaired file and a reference this demo can’t follow.</p>
    <div class="lab-fixtures js-only" role="group" aria-label="Choose a schema version">
      <button data-fixture="broken" aria-pressed="true"><span>01</span>Broken reference</button>
      <button data-fixture="repaired" aria-pressed="false"><span>02</span>Restore the definition</button>
      <button data-fixture="unsupported" aria-pressed="false"><span>03</span>External reference</button>
    </div>
    <p class="lab-hint js-only">The first file is broken on purpose. Running it should return <strong>EXIT 1 / SS-REF-001</strong>. Choose “Restore the definition” to see the passing example.</p>
    <div class="schema-lab">
      <div class="lab-input-panel">
        <div class="lab-panel-label mono"><span>INPUT / TOOLS.JSON</span><span data-fixture-label>BROKEN ON PURPOSE</span></div>
        <pre class="lab-code"><code data-fixture-code>{JSON.stringify({ name: 'get_weather', inputSchema: { type: 'object', properties: { location: { $ref: '#/$defs/Location' } }, required: ['location'] } }, null, 2)}</code></pre>
        <div class="lab-input-footer"><span class="mono">READ-ONLY EXAMPLE</span><button class="button button-gold js-only" data-run-fixture>RUN THE CHECK <Icon name="play" size={18} /></button></div>
      </div>
      <div class="lab-output-panel">
        <div class="lab-panel-label mono"><span>RESULT</span><span>LOCAL DEMO</span></div>
        <div class="lab-result" data-lab-result role="status" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"><span class="result-symbol" aria-hidden="true">?</span><h3>Ready to inspect.</h3><p>Run the check to find the missing definition. This example should produce a finding.</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
    <noscript><p class="noscript-note">The first file has a reference with no matching definition. JavaScript enables the three interactive examples. The <a href="/work/schema-sentinel/">project write-up</a> explains the full checker.</p></noscript>
    <div class="lab-scope"><span class="mono">WHAT IS RUNNING HERE?</span><p>A browser-only explanation using three fixed examples. It checks one reference. The full SchemaSentinel CLI has three rules, input validation, and additional unsupported-feature checks.</p></div>
    <div class="lab-lessons">
      <div><span class="mono">01 / THE FAILURE</span><h3>A reference needs a target.</h3><p>If an export keeps a <code>$ref</code> but drops its <code>$defs</code>, the input definition is incomplete. That is the defect this example shows.</p></div>
      <div><span class="mono">02 / THE LIMIT</span><h3>Can’t check is a separate result.</h3><p>An external file is outside this demo’s scope. Exit 2 keeps that situation separate from finding a bug or completing a check.</p></div>
      <div><span class="mono">03 / THE REPAIR</span><h3>Put the definition back.</h3><p>The second example restores <code>Location</code>. The reference resolves, so this particular check has no finding.</p></div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
<script>
  import '../../scripts/lab';
</script>
